**
!api/app/**
!api/static/**
!scripts/vps/api-requirements.lock

# Never build macOS AppleDouble resource forks into the image. They appear when a source tree is
# transferred with macOS tar/scp (the archive carries a ._<name> sidecar per file), and once present
# they are copied in alongside the real modules. They are inert -- Python never imports them, and
# every one carries the AppleDouble magic 00051607 -- but they made the running image's /srv/app
# differ from the host source in a way that looked like drift, and would make a clean rebuild
# produce a different image from the one serving traffic. The running image carries 179 of them.
**/._*
**/.DS_Store
